<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viljandi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fellin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Viljandi is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, on a lake in the old land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagala">Sakala</a>. Its hillfort was a chief stronghold of the Sakalians until German crusaders captured it in the 1210s and finally in 1224, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> built Fellin castle there, one of the largest castles of the order in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>. The town later joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/viljandi.jpg" alt="Viljandi" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vaido Otsar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viljandi_raekoda_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
